# TASK-260715-1idq8c outcome

## Delivered
- Added ReluxAppleUITestShared as the single source for BEM-like identifiers, typed launch arguments and environment, timeouts, and 18 deterministic fixtures covering profile, trust, capability, failure, diagnostic, onboarding, migration, and privacy states.
- Added isolated macOS and iOS Simulator fixture hosts plus two shared-source UI-test targets. The fixture graph has no NetworkExtension, production adapter, provider, VPN preference, credential, or network-client dependency.
- Added PageElement and ComponentElement protocols, PageManager composition, descriptive condition-based waits and actions, step-named XCTAttachments, xcresult extraction, controlled snapshot diff tooling, Swift Testing coverage, and physical-device/visual-review documentation. No Allure and no Designed-for-iPad Mac UI testing were added.

## Acceptance evidence
1. Shared source compiles through the macOS containing app anchor, both fixture hosts, and both UI-test targets. The iOS Simulator test passed; the native macOS fixture host/test bundle compiled before runner bootstrap. Static contract rejects raw RELUX_UI_TEST key duplication.
2. Page Objects use waitForExistence and XCTest predicate expectations. Static contract rejects Thread.sleep, sleep, and usleep in the UI infrastructure.
3. All 18 typed fixtures round-trip through the fail-closed launch parser. Launch is rejected without the explicit disabled network boundary. Values are synthetic and non-secret.
4. Final aggregate artifacts: .temp/TASK-260715-1idq8c/apple-ui-test/run.P4Md6k. iOS Simulator xcodebuild exit 0, one test passed, xcresult present, two step PNGs extracted. Controlled snapshot mismatch exit 1 as expected and emitted reference.png, failed.png, and diff.png. Native macOS xcodebuild exit 65: runner killed before bootstrap, zero test bodies passed. Overall smoke exit 1.
5. docs/apple-ui-test-validation.md makes orientation, layout, content, and black-screen review mandatory and defines separate TASK-<row-id>_physical-apple-ui-evidence.md ownership.

## Commands and exits
- swift format lint on all changed Swift inputs: 0.
- python3 -m py_compile for new Python tools and sh -n for smoke shell: 0.
- make apple-ui-test-contract: 0.
- make workspace-validate: 0.
- make macos-targets-validate: 0.
- swift test: 0, 455 tests passed with 25 pre-existing recorded known issues.
- swift build: 0.
- make apple-ui-test-smoke equivalent final run: 1 overall; macOS 65, iOS Simulator 0, controlled snapshot mismatch 1.
- read-only codesign strict verification of the assembled macOS runner: 1 with code resources/signature mismatch; no signing mutation was performed.

## Mandatory visual review
Final iOS Simulator Step_01 diagnostic fixture ready and Step_02 diagnostic fixture confirmed images were opened at original resolution. Both pass portrait orientation, centered unclipped layout, readable expected content, and non-black/non-empty rendering checks. The controlled diff image was opened and visibly highlights the mismatch.

## Safety and privacy
No signing, notarization, product/provider installation or launch, NetworkExtension approval, VPN preference creation/save/enable/start, route, DNS, interface, or packet-filter mutation occurred. Device identifiers and signing material are redacted from this outcome. The UI scheme never builds the provider.

## Stop-The-Line blocker and residual risk
Constraint: AC4 requires a native macOS XCUITest smoke, while the binding execution brief forbids signing on this workstation. Evidence: with CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO and CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO the complete runner/test/fixture graph compiles, but macOS kills the assembled runner before XCTest establishes a connection; xcresult records Early unexpected exit and signal kill. Strict signature verification reports that runner resources do not satisfy the retained signature. Repeating the unsigned run produces the same bootstrap class of failure.

Options: A) Recommended: run ReluxProxyMacUITests in a separately authorized test-only macOS signing lane, still using the non-networked fixture graph and never building or launching the provider. This preserves AC4 and the host boundary. B) Owner explicitly changes AC4 for this build-only lane to unsigned build-for-testing evidence and assigns native runtime proof to a named downstream signed-lane task. This weakens current-task runtime evidence. C) Authorize ad-hoc re-signing on this workstation. This conflicts with the binding brief and was not attempted.

Exact input needed: either authorize/provide a separate macOS lane permitted to sign and execute only the fixture host/XCUITest runner, or approve an acceptance change moving native macOS runtime proof to a named signed-lane task. Until then AC4 and the full smoke gate remain failing; no developer handoff is claimed.
